                     UNIVERSITY OF VICTORIA POLICY GUIDE
 
                                  Number 65
            Authorized April 14, 1986 (Revised 10 November 1992)
 
                       COMPUTING USER RESPONSIBILITIES
 
 INTRODUCTION
 The University of Victoria is responsible for ensuring that funds and other
 resources provided for the purpose of supporting University authorized
 teaching, research, administrative and other University computing
 activities are in fact used for those purposes.  Computing services and
 facilities are made available to departments and individuals through a
 process of budget allocations, and departments are then responsible for
 managing their computing budgets and, where appropriate, allocating
 computing funds to individual users.  All students, faculty and staff usage
 of computing services and facilities, funded by the University, must be
 authorized and approved within this framework.
 
 The following statements are intended to secure responsible use of the
 University computing services and facilities by all users.
 
 RESPONSIBILITIES
 As a condition of access to computing services and facilities, a user
 agrees:
 
 * not to compromise the integrity of any computing system by attempting
   access or alteration of system control programs or files;
 
 * not to use any computing system or user account unless formally and
   explicitly authorized to do so;
 
 * not to seek by any means copies of, or information regarding passwords,
   data, or programs of another user unless explicitly authorized to do so
   by that user;
 
 * not to alter charges levied by Computing and Systems Services for
   computing services or facilities;
 
 * not to harass other users of computing services or facilities;
 
 * not to use any University computing service or facility for
   non-University projects;
 
 * not to use any University computing service or facility for commercial
   purposes;
 
 * not to attempt to disrupt any computing service or facility;
 
 * not to use unlicensed or unauthorized copies of computer software;
 
 * to take all reasonable precautions to minimize opportunities for other
   persons to obtain access to passwords and files.
 
 ABUSE OF RESPONSIBILITIES
 Abuse or misuse of computing services or facilities may not only be a
 violation of user responsibilities but also of the Criminal Code.  Such
 violations may include the input of textual or graphical materials which
 could reasonably be questioned as a violation of Criminal Code provisions
 respecting pornography.  Therefore, the University will take appropriate
 action in response to user abuse or misuse of computing services or
 facilities, which action may include, but not necessarily be limited to:
 
 * withdrawal of computing privileges;
 
 * laying of charges under the Criminal Code.
 
 In connection with inquiries of possible abuses, it may be required to
 examine user files, programs, passwords, accounting information, printouts,
 or other computing materials, as enabled or permitted under the law.

